weekly to an optimal dose (maximum dose of 52.3/10.4 mg). During the double-blind Treatment Phase, subjects were 
randomized to receive their optimal dose of SDX/d-MPH or placebo for 7 days. On day 7, efficacy was assessed in the 
laboratory classroom using the Swanson, Kotkin, Agler, M-Flynn, and Pelham (SKAMP) Rating Scale and Permanent Product 
Measure of Performance (PERMP). To evaluate safety, adverse events (AEs), vital signs, and electrocardiograms were 
assessed, and suicide risk was assessed. Results: A total of 149 subjects completed the study. In the primary efficacy 
