disorder (ADHD). RESULTS ADHD pediatric outpatients (n = 253) diagnosed according to Diagnostic and Statistical Manual  
of Mental Disorders, 4(th) edition, criteria were randomized (1:1:1:1) to receive d-MPH XR (10, 20, or 30 mg o.d.) or   
placebo. Treatment with d-MPH XR significantly (p < 0.001) reduced the mean score (change from baseline) on             
Conners\'-ADHD/DSM-IV Scales (CADS) as assessed by the teacher CADS-T (dose [mean];10 mg [18], 20 mg [16.9], 30 mg      
