73%). Conversely, fewer ceiling effects were observed for the psychosocial scales (range 3-17% behaviour-parental       
emotional impact). The item-scaling results obtained in these pilot studies support the psychometric properties of the  
American-English CHQ-PF50 and its respective translations."}, {"study_index": 200, "title": "Response to comments on    
